{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - Access Control - Trusted Origin - Okta Trusted Origin Created or Modified",
	"Description": "A trusted origin was created, modified, or activated. Trusted origins are the CORS and redirect allowlist for your Okta org: adding an origin the adversary controls lets a page they host talk to the Okta API with a victim's session, which is the setup step for token theft.\n\nEvent types: security.trusted_origin.create, security.trusted_origin.update, security.trusted_origin.activate\n\nReference(s):\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/api/trusted-origins/\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/api/event-types/\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
